{"repositoryId":929472980,"availability":"available","full":"jakoch/php-wasm-devbox","name":"php-wasm-devbox","description":"A Docker-based devcontainer for building and deploying the PHP-WASM module. Also a language playground like 3v4l.org, but in the browser and served via Github Pages.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-02-08T16:22:52Z","updated":"2026-10-15T20:26:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jakoch.github.io/php-wasm-devbox/","topics":["docker","emscripten","php","playground","wasm"],"demo":"https://jakoch.github.io/php-wasm-devbox/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:01.004Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:01.004Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:52:01.004Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T15:52:01.004Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repository provides a streamlined development environment for building and deploying the PHP-WASM module.","It builds upon Derick Rethans php-wasm-builder, using its Dockerfile and phpw.c source file as a foundation. From there, I made extensive modifications to enhance flexibility, efficiency, and automation.","PHP-WASM is a WebAssembly module that runs PHP directly in the browser, compiled using Emscripten. It eliminates the need for a server, allowing PHP code to execute entirely on the client side."],"features":["Devcontainer support: Seamless PHP-WASM development using VSCode or any Devcontainer-compatible editor.","Multi-stage Dockerfile:","Build stage: Customizable compilation settings for PHP-WASM.","Deploy stage: Minimal, production-ready image based on Debian Trixie-slim.","PHP Language Playground: Provides a small language playground which is released to Github Pages."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jakoch/php-wasm-devbox/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"89ff3ea53722245ff323bec2eec01244fcc64d3e68fcad9f98a2dfbfb2e87ddb","extractedAt